Let $H$ = actually HIV$^+$. $P(H)=0.10$, $P(H^c)=0.90$.
Sensitivity $P(T^+|H)=0.95$; false-positive rate $P(T^+|H^c)=1-0.89=0.11$.

By Bayes' theorem:

$$P(H|T^+) = \frac{P(T^+|H)P(H)}{P(T^+|H)P(H)+P(T^+|H^c)P(H^c)}
= \frac{0.95\times0.10}{0.95\times0.10+0.11\times0.90}
= \frac{0.095}{0.095+0.099}
= \frac{0.095}{0.194}\approx 0.4897.$$

This is consistent with the official key value $0.485$ (rounded).
